          "type": "output_text",
          "text": "## Review outcome: event-level conclusion remains unverified\n\nI identified the relevant work order and September Pending Close cutoff, but the authorized records did not include cost-event rows needed to complete the investigation.\n\n| Requested item | Verified result |\n|---|---|\n| Manufacturing order | **MO-25-09-1070** |\n| Work order ID | **WO-2025-09-004** |\n| Operation / product | Modine Racine–DeKoven / Cooler Plate Pack |\n| Cost period | **Sep-25 — PER-COST-2025-09** |\n| Exact Pending Close time | **2025-09-30T18:00:00** |\n| Source transaction ID | Not verifiable from accessible records |\n| Event amount | Not verifiable |\n| Exact event-created time | Not verifiable |\n| Minutes after Pending Close | Cannot calculate without the event-created time |\n| Recorded accounting status | Not verifiable |\n| Status consistent with Oracle policy? | **Undetermined** |\n\nThe timestamp above is reproduced exactly; the source does not specify a timezone.\n\n### Oracle’s documented treatment\n\nOracle Fusion Cloud SCM Cost Management 26B states that, while a period is **Pending Close**, newly created transactions falling in that period or an earlier period **are not staged in Cost Accounting or Receipt Accounting**. They are processed after the period is closed or reopened. Transactions entered before Pending Close continue processing, including those in error. **Revenue lines, COGS recognition, and manual cost adjustments are exceptions** that continue processing after Pending Close.\n\nSource: *Cost Accounting Period Statuses and Transaction Accounting*, PDF page 233, printed page 225.\n\nThus, an ordinary new transaction created after **2025-09-30T18:00:00** should be held from processing while September remains Pending Close. Assessing an actual event’s recorded status requires its type, creation time, and status.\n\n### Evidence limitation\n\nThe accessible source contained **24 work-order rows and five cost-period rows, but no cost-event rows**. Supporting records were restricted to the records-custodian role and were not accessed. Therefore, this is **not a finding that no late event occurred**; the existence of a late event and its accounting treatment remain unverified.\n\nNo business database records were changed. The audit result and provenance were saved to `/cache/work/worker_d1f5fc8ad4e3/audit-report.json`; the submitted report is marked **needs_evidence**.",
          "annotations": [],
          "logprobs": []
        }
      ],
      "phase": "final_answer"
    }
